ion. During this stage, the model learns to effectively leverage accumulated cross-modal context for temporally coherent generation. Finally, to further improve the overall generation performance, we apply online reinforcement post-training (Xue et al. 2025 ) adapted for joint streaming audio-video generation, with reward signals targeting audio-visual quality, synchronization, and speech alignment. \nOur contributions are threefold. (1) We develop a three-stage training paradigm that effectively transfers a bidirectional audio-video generation teacher into a causal streaming generator, comprising three stages: memory-augmented block-causal adap", "stderr": "\nShell cwd was reset to /inspire/qb-ilm/project/video-generation/chenxie-25019/hyr/iHateTheWorld555.github.io", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
